 =?UTF-8?q?=D0=BE=D0=BC=D1=81=D0=BA=D0=B8=D0=B9?= <git@igrnt.info>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:27:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1053/1252] Karaoke timing; the studio's own dialogs and
 dropdowns; datasheet; cards, trash, chain
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1056: karaoke timing in the Lyrics step: Whisper with word times, the lyric
lines aligned to the heard words, a line too little heard placed between its
neighbours and marked guessed; .lrc and .srt; a click on a time plays there.
1057: every browser confirm() and prompt() (30 of them) is the studio's own
dialog: title and explanation, Enter yes, Esc no.
1058: every dropdown in the studio's dress (a drawn chevron); cards keep one
height: a note is a mark at the end of the row, its words on hover; the card
that sounds pulses; "Not in a workspace" on the left; the trash: Select all,
Clear, "Wipe out the trash" (or "Delete N for good" when some are ticked),
its term on one line.
1059: the menu offers the other rooms only ("Open in Collection" shows the
take there, flashed); "Open the datasheet": everything a take was made with
(style, lyrics, score, mode, seeds, sampling, sliders, LoRAs, the request as
JSON) without leaving the room; the chain shows its progress ("Enjoy the
magic… 2 / 5") and Artifacts turns to its final file when done; remaster
lengths in the tree; the player fits a narrow or zoomed window again (the
1042 rule had undone the 1150 px query).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
